---@field place_route fun(region:integer, start:number[], end_:number[], start_node?:MT2Handle, end_node?:MT2Handle, start_split?:MT2Handle, end_split?:MT2Handle):MT2Action Execute the whole original native Road hover/pin/Press transaction, accepting native auto snapping, split targets and up to ten native preview splines. Returns all created Paths/nodes, changed Path before/after values, removed Paths, cost, native spline count and owned history receipt. Native geometry and mixed topology readback own the result; one final Press follows only an acknowledged no-effect pin phase.
---@field graph fun():MT2PathGraph Read the complete saved root-world mixed Path graph, including all eleven Path types, six Intersection types, reciprocal node edges and cross-Region membership. Fields contain native handles, Region IDs, names, waypoints and native distances.
---@field place fun(region:integer, start:number[], end_:number[], start_node?:MT2Handle, end_node?:MT2Handle):MT2Action Create one native Road segment through an isolated original Road cursor hover/press, native purchase and Undo. Native ground projection sets endpoint height; optional native node handles pin connections. Splitting existing Paths and multi-spline Road previews are rejected. Returns the created Path, cost and owned history receipt; normal native costs and tool effects apply.
---@field link fun(start_region:integer, end_region:integer, name:string, start:number[], end_:number[], start_node?:MT2Handle, end_node?:MT2Handle):MT2Action Create a native cross-Region Pass through an isolated original Pass receiver and Finish transaction. Confirms both Regions, supplied two-point shape, endpoint identities, remote membership and native Undo. Returns the Pass and owned history receipt; normal native tool effects apply.
---@field remove fun(handle:MT2Handle):MT2Action Remove any current mixed Path, including Wall or Pass, through original native Destroy command and edit transaction. Confirms Path removal, native orphan policy for endpoint types0/1, retained other Intersections, remote/selection retirement and exact Make/Cash inverse UID set. Returns refund, removed node count and owned history receipt.
---@field undo fun(receipt:string):MT2Action Run original native undo for one owned Path/Wall receipt at the exact native stack top. Confirms the complete saved mixed topology and exact source/inverse stack transition. Up to twenty receipts are retained in the current World lifetime; an unresolved native history attempt quarantines its receipt.
---@field redo fun(receipt:string):MT2Action Run original native redo for one owned Path/Wall receipt at the exact native stack top. Confirms the complete saved mixed topology and exact source/inverse stack transition. Up to twenty receipts are retained in the current World lifetime; an unresolved native history attempt quarantines its receipt.

---@class MT2ProjectsAPI
---@field catalogue fun():MT2ProjectCatalogueRow[] Read native project eligibility and technology purchase/deployment flags
---@field current fun():MT2ProjectProgress Read current source, work, code lines, bugs and desired workers
---@field start fun(source:MT2ProjectSource):MT2Action Pay for and start the selected native research, art, statistic or shared project source
---@field cancel fun():MT2Action Cancel and retire the current native project
---@field commit fun():MT2Action Deploy and retire the natively completed current project
---@field set_workers fun(count:integer):MT2Action Allocate workers to the current native project
---@field get fun(source:MT2ProjectSource):MT2ProjectCatalogueRow Read the current availability, price and worker limit for one project source.

---@class MT2QuestsAPI
---@field list fun(handle:MT2ActorHandle):MT2NpcQuest[] Read a QuestGiver NPC's owned quest slots, authored fields, destination handles and daily counters with reciprocal weak ownership checks.
---@field get fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle):MT2NpcQuest Read a quest only while its exact current owner, slot and sequence still match.
---@field create fun(handle:MT2ActorHandle):MT2Action Generate and append a native quest for a QuestGiver with fewer than five quests and an existing Building fallback destination. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field remove fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle):MT2Action Remove a current quest through native NPC lifetime cleanup and verify its expired visitor references and reindexed survivors. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field swap fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle, slot:integer):MT2Action Swap two quest slots through native ReorderQuest and confirm the complete owner/global records. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field set_name fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle, name:string):MT2Action Assign the quest title through the native String method. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field set_kills fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle, kills:integer):MT2Action Set the authored kill count with the original selector's field semantics. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field set_rewards fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle, defaults?:boolean, xp?:integer, gold?:integer):MT2Action Set custom or default awards through the original native reward setters. Preserve the original native Undo inverse, active visitor state and ledger with complete readback.
---@field set_destination fun(handle:MT2NpcQuestHandle, destination:MT2Handle, kills?:integer):MT2Action Run original SetDestination with the native default action, then verify all global quest records, reciprocal weak links, its single-operation native Undo inverse, recalculation task and unchanged ledger.

---@class MT2RegionsAPI
---@field set_type fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, type:integer, position:number[]):MT2Action Apply the original private Lift/Land transaction to an unowned Region, clear its native contents and retain the original Undo graph.
---@field list fun(offset?:integer, limit?:integer):MT2RegionPage List saved root-world Region handles using bounded pages.
---@field get fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle):MT2RegionDetails Read a Region name, type, levels, styles and complete environment settings.
---@field presets fun():string[] Read the native Region preset names.
---@field rename fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, name:string):MT2Action Rename a Region through its native widget notification.
---@field set_tint fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, values:number[]):MT2Action Set the native Region tint.
---@field set_light fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, values:number[]):MT2Action Set native Region light.
---@field set_ambient fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, values:number[]):MT2Action Set native Region ambient light.
---@field set_sky fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, values:number[]):MT2Action Set native Region sky spline coefficients.
---@field set_particles fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, type:integer):MT2Action Set the original Region particle type and enabled state.
---@field set_particle_color fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, values:number[]):MT2Action Set the original Region particle color.
---@field styles fun():string[] Read the nine canonical terrain style names.
---@field set_styles fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, styles:string[]):MT2Action Apply all four terrain styles through the original native EditManager transaction.
---@field set_levels fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, minimum:integer, maximum:integer, position?:number[]):MT2Action Set the Region level range with the original tool transaction, complete actor level clamp, restored input and native Undo inverse.
---@field set_preset fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, name:string):MT2Action Apply an original Region preset, confirm its styles and refresh the visible native inspector.
---@field purchase fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, position?:number[]):MT2Action Buy unowned land through the original native tool, with complete actor level clamp, payment and inverse readback.
---@field sell fun(handle:MT2RegionHandle, position?:number[]):MT2Action Sell owned land through the original native tool, with complete actor level clamp, refund and inverse readback.
---@field at fun(x:number, z:number):MT2RegionHandle|nil Find the saved root Region at a world position; return nil outside the map.

---@class MT2SceneryAPI
---@field stroke fun(kind:string, region:integer, finish_position:number[], stamps:MT2SceneryStrokeStamp[], type?:string, variant?:string, random_variant?:boolean, replace?:boolean, bounds?:number[]):MT2Action Run complete ordered native SceneryBrush or SceneryEraser AddPaint stamps and one original Finish through isolated private receivers. Returns created/removed Scenery rows, cumulative birth count, paid/refund amounts and before/after Building/Monster bug-anchor records. Confirms complete born/removed full-UID Make/Destroy/cash inverse coverage, saved Make records, unchanged surviving Scenery, Group member removals and native Release edits. Preserves normal native cost, replacement, variant RNG and brush bug effects; confirms general erase leaves RNG/bugs unchanged. Temporarily journals the original Cursor finish position and restores it plus surviving selection. Requires the root world to be the actual native active scene. Partial native owners are retained on uncertain failures; never replay such a result.
---@field transform fun(targets:MT2SceneryTransform[]):MT2Action Move, rotate or scale multiple free Scenery in one original native Begin/Open/DoMove-per-target/Close/End transaction. Returns target results in input order. Confirms exact inverse UID/prior-pose order, destination Region, unchanged other Scenery and unchanged Groups. Requires the root world to be the actual active scene and owned destination Regions; normal native tool effects apply.
---@field duplicate fun(handle:MT2Handle, position:number[], rotation?:number[], scale?:number[]):MT2Action Duplicate free Scenery or a whole Group through original native capability/price/payment, virtual Duplicate, cash/destroy inverses and localized Undo. Confirms created pose, whole Group member ordering/relative poses and untouched sources, plus native release edit and selection readback. Returns a Scenery prop or Group table. Requires the root world to be the native active scene; normal native costs and selection changes apply.
---@field list fun():MT2SceneryProp[] Read current root-world Scenery handles, native poses and Region IDs from every actual Region/category roster. A pose contains quaternion x/y/z/w, position x/y/z and scale x/y/z, in that order.
---@field move_group fun(group:MT2Handle, position:number[], rotation?:number[], scale?:number[]):MT2Action Move, rotate or scale a whole native Group through original DoMove and Undo, preserving its ordered member identities and relative poses. Confirms native destination pose and unchanged other Groups/Scenery. Requires the root world to be the actual native active scene; normal native selection and tool effects apply.
---@field destroy_group fun(group:MT2Handle):MT2Action Destroy a whole native Group through original SelectionManager DestroyProp, retaining normal native refund and Undo behavior. Confirms removal of the Group and every owned Scenery member, plus unchanged unrelated members. Returns destroyed=true and member count. Requires the root world to be the actual native active scene; normal native selection and tool effects apply.
---@field groups fun():MT2SceneryGroup[] Read root-world Groups with exact Group and member handles, native ten-float poses, Region IDs and relative member poses.
---@field group fun(handles:MT2Handle[]):MT2Action Group or merge root-world Scenery through explicitly rooted native Group creation and the whole original GroupSelection transaction. Confirms ordered membership, unchanged member poses, reciprocal parents and exact native Undo. Requires the root world to be the native active scene and the current native tool to permit selection; normal native selection changes apply.
---@field ungroup fun(handles:MT2Handle[]):MT2Action Run the whole original UngroupSelection transaction and confirm removal, free surviving member handles and unchanged member poses, plus original per-Group saved inverse records. Returns ungrouped count and members. Requires the root world to be the native active scene and the current native tool to permit selection; normal native selection changes apply.

